%erg 0.1
Title: test_encoding.sh ignores TMPDIR and halts make check on a full /tmp
Created: 2026-09-16
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-16T12:14Z claude created

--- body ---

## Context

Found during ticket 0278's integration pass (PR #352), by a reviewer whose
`/tmp` was a full tmpfs. `tests/test_encoding.sh:155` is the only suite in the
repo that hardcodes `/tmp` in its `mktemp` call:

    TMPFFFD=$(mktemp /tmp/test_encoding_fffd_negctrl_XXXXXX.txt)

Every other suite uses a bare `mktemp -d`, which honours `TMPDIR`. So on a host
whose `/tmp` is small, full, read-only or absent, `make check` halts inside
`test-encoding` regardless of where the operator pointed `TMPDIR` -- and it
halts at the FIRST failing target, so every suite ordered after it never runs.
The operator's one lever for the condition does not reach the one suite that
ignores it.

Severity: it blocks the pre-PR gate, and the failure reads as an encoding-guard
failure rather than as "the disk is full", so the diagnosis costs more than the
fix.

Not a defect PR #352 introduced, and not in 0278's scope -- filed rather than
fixed inline so the change lands as its own reviewable diff.

## Relevant files

- `tests/test_encoding.sh` -- line 155, the U+FFFD negative-control temp file

## Actions

1. Drop the hardcoded directory: `mktemp` with a bare template (or `mktemp -t`)
   so `TMPDIR` applies, matching every sibling suite.
2. Sweep the rest of `tests/` for the same shape before closing -- a rename or
   refactor sweep covers the smallest containing unit, which here is the suite
   directory. (`tests/test_version.sh:28` mentions `/tmp/tickets/erg` inside
   expected OUTPUT text, not a path it writes; that one is not this defect.)

## Test

Red step: run the suite with `TMPDIR` pointed at a known directory and assert
the scratch file lands under it. Today it lands in `/tmp` and the assertion
fails. A cheaper mechanical form, if a per-suite test is disproportionate: a
grep ratchet asserting no `mktemp` under `tests/` names an absolute directory.

## Verification

- [ ] `TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d) make test-encoding` writes no file under `/tmp`
- [ ] `make check` still green

## Invariants

- The U+FFFD negative control must keep firing -- it is what makes the encoding
  guard non-vacuous. Moving where its temp file lives must not change whether
  the injected U+FFFD is detected.

## Exit criteria

- No suite under `tests/` hardcodes an absolute scratch directory
- `make check` green
